prompts.tables_json:
Identify and extract the table schema
 Extract the schema of all the tables in the image sorted according to the reading order.
The output must be a valid JSON object containing a list of dictionaries with the following structure:

                {
                    "dimensions": {
                        "rows": <number of data rows (excluding header rows)>,
                        "columns": <number of columns>,
                        "header_rows": <number of header rows>,
                        "total_rows": <total number of rows including headers>
                    },
                    "cells": [
                        {
                        "row": <row index starting at 1>,
                        "col": <column index starting at 1>,
                        "colspan": <number of columns spanned>,
                        "rowspan": <number of rows spanned>,
                        "type": "<'header' or 'data'>",
                        "header_level": <header nesting level if type=header, else omit or null>,
                        "content": "<string content of the cell>"
                        },
                        ...
                    ]
                }
